  "title": "Impossible Metals is Collaborating with BGR to Test Its Hovering Selective Collection Robot for Collecting Critical Metals from the Seabed",
  "summary": "San Jose, California – Impossible Metals announces a collaboration with the German Federal Institute for Geosciences and Natural Resources (BGR) to pilot test its Eureka III selective collection autonomous underwater vehicle (AUV) for polymetallic nodule collection in the Clarion Clipperton Zone (CCZ). The four-day test will collect data regarding the technical feasibility",
